// ==UserScript==
// @name         Argon Survey Guard v13.5 (Access Control + Quiet Mode)
// @namespace    http://tampermonkey.net/
// !!! NEVER CHANGE @name OR @namespace AGAIN. Tampermonkey ties the saved data (Access ID, name, locks) to them.
// !!! A new @name = a NEW script = NEW Access ID + empty storage. Only change @version.
// @version      16.68
// @updateURL    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rohimgpt/argon-list/main/argon.user.js
// @downloadURL  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rohimgpt/argon-list/main/argon.user.js
// @description  v16.68: BLOCK SCREEN HARDENING (ideas from the extension) - tab title locked, scrolling disabled, red screen re-attached instantly if the site removes it, page address + Copy-link button on the block screen, local Blocked-history (last 50, menu command). v16.67: HARD REDIRECT LOCK - (1) once a page is blocked, EVERY navigation / form submit / click / window redirect (even to Lootwalls) is cancelled, so a blocked survey can never reach Lootwalls; (2) at the moment of ANY redirect, form submit or Submit/Next-button click a FRESH synchronous scan of the whole page (text, links, iframes, address, referrer, meta) runs with caches bypassed, and a hit cancels the redirect and shows the red screen at once; (3) beforeunload fallback for browsers without the Navigation API. v16.66: REDIRECT BLOCK ON ROUTER PAGES - (1) a redirect / form submit / meta refresh whose target contains a blocked word or domain is cancelled AND the red block screen is shown even on Router pages (before: only a notification, page stayed open and the survey could go on); on the Lootwalls page itself the navigation is only cancelled (so the offer list is never trapped); (2) redirect-chain memory now also works on Router pages, so the page that follows a blocked page is blocked too (15s); (3) the navigation guard + the address / referrer check start synchronously at document-start (no longer wait for the tab data), so the fastest redirects are caught; (4) <meta http-equiv=refresh> targets are checked. Lootwalls status pages are never blocked (completion still saves). v16.65: REPEAT CHECK USES ONLY THE FIRST PAGES on topic hosts (ShopperMX / Upside / nsv / UserTesting participant): topic + question keys are learned only from the first 6 pages of a survey, and a page with no answer controls (the shared last "Submit" page) is never learned, so it can no longer make a different survey look like a repeat. v16.64: FAST REDIRECTS - (1) the Navigation API sees where the page is ABOUT to go (JS / meta / form redirects) and cancels it when the target contains a blocked word; (2) a blocked address is remembered for 12s in this tab, so the next page of a redirect chain is blocked too; (3) the referrer is checked; (4) the address is checked synchronously before the tab data loads. Router / Lootwalls pages are exempt (completion still saves). v16.63: INSTANT BLOCK - blocklist is checked ~every 0.15s and on every page change (text, links, iframes, images, address changes), so even a 1-second appearance blocks; every address the page ever had (pushState/replaceState) is remembered and checked; the block is sticky until a newer admin list no longer matches; whole-page text is scanned (not only the top). v16.62: the address a page was OPENED with is remembered and checked too (survey sites that strip ?Platform=LUCID&... from the address bar after loading no longer slip through). v16.61: link reading rebuilt - links are fully decoded (double-encoded too); every blocked domain / keyword is matched ANYWHERE in the link (host, path, query, #hash, redirect parameter); multi-word keywords (big village, gauge insights, gfk 0, strat.7.audiences) match big-village / big_village / big%20village / bigvillage; domain rules with a path work; links inside Google/Facebook redirect wrappers are checked; up to 3000 links and href/action/data-* attributes are scanned. v16.60: blocked words (lucid, attest, potentia, gfk + the whole admin list) are matched ANYWHERE inside a URL (page link, iframe, every link on the page), even glued to other letters (lucidhq.com); lucide / attestation / potential stay allowed. v16.59: the thank-you -> Lootwalls completed window is 3 minutes (was 2). v16.58: a survey is added to the sheet and locked ONLY when Lootwalls status=completed is reached. A thank-you / completed page only starts a 2-minute window; Lootwalls completed inside it saves that session (with its topic), a different page or a late Lootwalls adds nothing. v16.57: surveygpt.com stays in the router list (dashboard never scanned / blocked); wider end-screen wording (thank you for participating, interview complete, response submitted...) so interview-style surveys such as Loops (app.useloops.com) are saved as completed. v16.56: FIX - a survey that ends on the SurveyGPT /dashboard page is saved to the sheet again (v16.55 skipped that page completely); the dashboard itself is still never blocked and gives no topic. surveygpt.com is no longer a router host. v16.55: surveygpt.com (SurveyGPT portal) is treated as a survey-wall like freecash/swagbucks and any /dashboard page is never scanned, so the red "already completed" screen no longer appears on the dashboard. v16.54: a page whose questions are ALL profile questions gives no topic and is not counted in the first 4 topic pages (title/heading included); wider profile wording (home own/rent, military, religion, insurance, pets, income...). v16.53: topic hosts (Upside, ShopperMX, nsv.netr.jp, UserTesting participant) capture more topic phrases (up to 10 keys, 16 phrases per page). v16.52: profile questions AND their answer options (age, income, gender, employment, education, race, countries/states) are stripped from the page text before topic detection, in all surveys (Upside / ShopperMX first pages no longer become the topic). v16.51: host-scoped keywords ("surveymonkey.com::consumer") block only on that domain, when the word is in the first 4 pages of the survey. v16.49: location questions ("In which state or territory?") and their answers (countries / UK nations / states) are profile questions and never become the topic. Locks a completed survey for 7/15/30 days, tracks real start-to-end time, merge-able backups, admin-controlled remote blocklist (domains / keywords / logo images, also checked inside page links, headers, titles & logos), and an approval system (Pending / Allowed / Blocked access IDs). v16.48: UserTesting completed only via Lootwalls status=completed. v16.47: UserTesting one-page surveys are completed through Lootwalls status=completed (no thank-you text rule). v16.45: participant.use2.usertesting.com is a topic host (like ShopperMX). v16.44: UserTesting qualify page is not completed; nsv.netr.jp topic host. v16.43: better topic detection (brand names, purchase phrases, platform words ignored, word-order/plural-proof keys on Upside+ShopperMX). v16.42: Upside=start.dig.one, ShopperMX=incontext.decipherinc.com, link/id ignored, topic required. v16.41: Upside+ShopperMX strict topic matching (per-survey ratio, generic keys ignored). v16.40: topic from first 4 non-profile pages (all surveys), topic-first repeat check, 1-page surveys. v16.39: Upside topic. v16.38: repeat detected by topic when the link/id changes. v16.37: sheet has survey links only (no Lootwalls / UT screener rows). v16.36: CSV hides apiKey/userId. v16.35: UserTesting screener/legal steps no longer logged as completed. v16.34: strict-keyword and storage-lock fixes. v16.12: fixed scan crash (null.startsWith) that stopped NEW-survey alerts; admin block screen now replaces the whole page so the red screen always shows.
// @match        *://*/*
// @noframes
